{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Addendum — the full unit sweep did complete, and it is clean\n\nThe earlier report recorded the full-tree run as an accepted residual risk because the host was\nsaturated. It has since finished:\n\n    11992 passed, 44 skipped, 1 warning, 2 errors in 2177.17s\n\nBoth `errors` are **self-inflicted concurrency artifacts, not defects** — I committed while that\nsuite was still running in the background:\n\n* `test_compact_all_selection.py` — *New entries appeared in REPO_ROOT during this test:\n  ['COMMITMSG.tmp']* — my temporary commit-message file, created and deleted mid-run.\n* `test_compact_crash_atomicity.py` — *Test moved the repo HEAD (fe9401b1d7 -> cfbdbd3138)* — my\n  own commit landing mid-run.\n\nBoth were **re-run on a quiet tree and pass: 33 passed**. So the sweep is 11992 passed with zero\nreal failures, and the residual risk recorded earlier is discharged.\n\nWorth noting what those two messages demonstrate: the guards named an **external** cause instead\nof blaming the straddling test. That is bug `f0fb-de7a-b315-4508`'s diagnostic fix working — the\nsame fix whose Step-7 sweep produced this ticket. A pleasing confirmation that the class of work\npays off in exactly the way it was argued it would.\n\nGerrit **1989**: `LLM-Review +1` (PASS). `Verified` still running."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787305231556359001,"uuid":"6e803d11-b6bf-495c-a3ac-1b829d3c42fb"}